> Using Tax_rates as T
> Using Types

# Tests for the Tax_rates module (issue #10)

Run with `clerk test`. Expected values were computed by an independent
Python reference (exact `Decimal` arithmetic, midpoint rule of scope.md
section 2.1, cumulative "$B plus R%" form, round half up) and, below $100,000,
agree with the printed Tax Table (`test_tax_rates_table.catala_en`, 2,060 rows
times 4 statuses) and with Direct File's engine values
(`test_tax_rates_oracle.catala_en`).

## Midpoint (Direct File `/roundedTaxableIncome`)

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRoundedTaxableIncome:
  output ok condition

scope TestRoundedTaxableIncome:
  rule ok fulfilled
  # at most zero
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $0) = $0
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of -$100) = $0
  # the three hard-coded midpoints under $25
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $0.01) = $2.50
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $4.99) = $2.50
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $5) = $10
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $14.99) = $10
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $15) = $20
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $24.99) = $20
  # $25 rows up to $3,000: row [25, 50) has midpoint 37.50
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $25) = $37.50
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $49.99) = $37.50
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $50) = $62.50
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $2,975) = $2,987.50
  # last $25 row and first $50 row
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $2,999.99) = $2,987.50
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $3,000) = $3,025
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $3,049.99) = $3,025
  # last $50 row, then the exact income
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $99,999) = $99,975
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $100,000) = $100,000
  assertion (T.rounded_taxable_income_of of $123,456.78) = $123,456.78
```

## Line 16, single: the issue's named cases

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestTentativeTaxSingleBoundaries:
  output ok condition

scope TestTentativeTaxSingleBoundaries:
  rule ok fulfilled
  # TI 0 gives 0; TI 4 is taxed as 2.50: 10% of 2.50 = 0.25, rounded to 0
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $0, Single) = $0
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $4, Single) = $0
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $5, Single) = $1
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $15, Single) = $2
  # rows around 15,000: [14,950, 15,000) and [15,000, 15,050)
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $14,999, Single) = $1,565
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $15,000, Single) = $1,571
  # $25 rows to $50 rows
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $2,999.99, Single) = $299
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $3,000, Single) = $303
  # midpoint to exact income
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $99,999, Single) = $17,048
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $100,000, Single) = $17,053
```

## One income in each of the seven brackets, for each schedule

The incomes are bracket midpoints (or $1,000 above the start of the top
bracket); the last line of each block is a 37% income of $10,000,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestTentativeTaxMarriedJointly:
  output ok condition

scope TestTentativeTaxMarriedJointly:
  rule ok fulfilled
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $11,600, MarriedFilingJointly) = $1,163
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $58,750, MarriedFilingJointly) = $6,589
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $147,675, MarriedFilingJointly) = $22,595
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $292,475, MarriedFilingJointly) = $56,279
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $435,675, MarriedFilingJointly) = $94,789
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $609,325, MarriedFilingJointly) = $154,013
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $732,200, MarriedFilingJointly) = $197,040
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $10,000,000, MarriedFilingJointly) = $3,626,126
  # bracket tops: 34,337 = 10,852 + 22% * (201,050 - 94,300);
  # 196,669.50 rounds half up to 196,670
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $201,050, MarriedFilingJointly) = $34,337
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $731,200, MarriedFilingJointly) = $196,670

#[test]
declaration scope TestTentativeTaxQualifyingSurvivingSpouse:
  output ok condition

scope TestTentativeTaxQualifyingSurvivingSpouse:
  # QSS uses the MFJ schedule (1(a), 2(a); DF: isFilingStatusMFJ or QSS)
  rule ok fulfilled
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $11,600, QualifyingSurvivingSpouse) = $1,163
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $147,675, QualifyingSurvivingSpouse) = $22,595
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $732,200, QualifyingSurvivingSpouse) = $197,040
  assertion (T.schedule_for of QualifyingSurvivingSpouse)
            = (T.schedule_for of MarriedFilingJointly)

#[test]
declaration scope TestTentativeTaxHeadOfHousehold:
  output ok condition

scope TestTentativeTaxHeadOfHousehold:
  rule ok fulfilled
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $8,275, HeadOfHousehold) = $828
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $39,825, HeadOfHousehold) = $4,448
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $81,800, HeadOfHousehold) = $11,361
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $146,225, HeadOfHousehold) = $26,443
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $217,825, HeadOfHousehold) = $45,697
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $426,525, HeadOfHousehold) = $117,966
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $610,350, HeadOfHousehold) = $182,325
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $10,000,000, HeadOfHousehold) = $3,656,495
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $609,350, HeadOfHousehold) = $181,955

#[test]
declaration scope TestTentativeTaxSingle:
  output ok condition

scope TestTentativeTaxSingle:
  rule ok fulfilled
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $5,800, Single) = $583
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $29,375, Single) = $3,293
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $73,837, Single) = $11,295
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $146,237, Single) = $28,139
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $217,837, Single) = $47,394
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $426,537, Single) = $119,663
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $610,350, Single) = $184,017
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $10,000,000, Single) = $3,658,188
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $609,350, Single) = $183,647

#[test]
declaration scope TestTentativeTaxMarriedSeparately:
  output ok condition

scope TestTentativeTaxMarriedSeparately:
  rule ok fulfilled
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $5,800, MarriedFilingSeparately) = $583
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $29,375, MarriedFilingSeparately) = $3,293
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $73,837, MarriedFilingSeparately) = $11,295
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $146,237, MarriedFilingSeparately) = $28,139
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $217,837, MarriedFilingSeparately) = $47,394
  # 35% bracket ends at 365,600 for MFS (609,350 for Single)
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $304,662, MarriedFilingSeparately) = $77,006
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $366,600, MarriedFilingSeparately) = $98,705
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $10,000,000, MarriedFilingSeparately) = $3,663,063
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $365,600, MarriedFilingSeparately) = $98,335
  # same income, Single is still in the 35% bracket
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $366,600, Single) = $98,685
```

## The scope itself, end to end

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestTentativeTaxScope:
  output ok condition
  internal run content T.TentativeTax

scope TestTentativeTaxScope:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition run equals
    output of T.TentativeTax with {
      -- taxable_income: $14,999 -- filing_status: Single
    }
  assertion run.rounded_taxable_income = $14,975
  assertion run.tentative_tax_from_taxable_income = $1,565
  assertion run.tentative_tax_cumulative_form = $1,565
```

## Rejecting bad outputs

The spec must not accept these wrong answers.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestBadOutputsRejected:
  output ok condition

scope TestBadOutputsRejected:
  rule ok fulfilled
  # Without the midpoint, the exact tax on 14,999 would be 1,568, not the
  # Tax Table's 1,565.
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $14,999, Single) != $1,568
  # Copying the Rev. Proc. 2023-34 typo ("excess over $191,150") for Single
  # at 200,000 would give 39,110.50 + 32% * 8,850 = 41,942.50 -> 41,943.
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $200,000, Single) = $41,687
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $200,000, Single) != $41,943
  # MFJ income 100,000 is not taxed on the Single schedule
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $100,000, MarriedFilingJointly)
            != (T.tentative_tax_for of $100,000, Single)
  # A flat 10% would be wrong above the first bracket
  assertion (T.tentative_tax_for of $50,000, Single) != $5,000
```

## The two forms agree; the bases chain

For every bracket after the first, the table's base amount equals the base
of the previous bracket plus its rate times its width, and the first bracket
starts at $0 with base $0. The marginal form and the cumulative form give the
same tax at every tested income, for all statuses.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestSchedulesChain:
  output ok condition
  internal all_tables content list of list of T.Bracket

scope TestSchedulesChain:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition all_tables equals [
    T.schedule_mfj_qss; T.schedule_head_of_household;
    T.schedule_single; T.schedule_married_separate ]
  assertion
    for all table among all_tables we have
      (for all b among table we have
         (b.lower = $0 and b.base = $0) or
         (exists p among table such that
            p.upper = b.lower and
            b.base = p.base + (p.upper - p.lower) * p.rate))
  # seven brackets, rates 10, 12, 22, 24, 32, 35, 37 in order
  assertion
    for all table among all_tables we have
      (map each b among table to b.rate)
      = [10%; 12%; 22%; 24%; 32%; 35%; 37%]
  # the top bracket is open-ended
  assertion
    for all table among all_tables we have
      (exists b among table such that b.upper = T.no_upper_bound)

#[test]
declaration scope TestFormsAgree:
  output ok condition
  internal incomes content list of money
  internal statuses content list of Types.FilingStatus

scope TestFormsAgree:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition incomes equals [
    $0; $4; $15; $25; $2,999.99; $3,000; $11,600; $11,650; $14,999; $23,200;
    $23,250; $47,150; $63,100; $94,300; $99,999; $100,000; $100,525; $100,500;
    $191,950; $201,050; $243,700; $243,725; $365,600; $383,900; $487,450;
    $609,350; $731,200; $1,234,567.89; $10,000,000 ]
  definition statuses equals [
    Single; MarriedFilingJointly; MarriedFilingSeparately;
    HeadOfHousehold; QualifyingSurvivingSpouse ]
  assertion
    for all s among statuses we have
      (for all x among incomes we have
        (T.tentative_tax_for of x, s) = (T.tentative_tax_cumulative_for of x, s))
  # QSS and MFJ coincide
  assertion
    for all x among incomes we have
      (T.tentative_tax_for of x, QualifyingSurvivingSpouse)
      = (T.tentative_tax_for of x, MarriedFilingJointly)
  # No taxable income, no tax, for every status
  assertion
    for all s among statuses we have
      (T.tentative_tax_for of $0, s) = $0
```
